<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06W8">Variant <span data-tag="06W8">9.6.6.7</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{A}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{B}}$ and $G: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be functors between (small) $\infty $-categories, where $F$ is categorically $n$-connective and $G$ is $n$-faithful. Then $F$ is left orthogonal to $G$ in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$. This follows from Corollary <a data-tag="05CH" href="/tag/05CH">4.8.5.23</a> (together with Example <a data-tag="06W6" href="/tag/06W6">9.6.6.5</a> and Proposition <a data-tag="033C" href="/tag/033C">4.5.3.15</a>). </p>
</article>
